msgid "Scenario VI: Bacchanalia"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"There's not a moment to lose now.  You make a tour of the city's newspaper stands and delve into the society pages.  If there's any big organization dedicated to Shub-Niggurath, it has to be exclusive, perhaps even secretive to avoid any ignorant socialite joining by mistake, and likely has some obvious connection only noticeable to those looking for it.  One name among the newspapers catches your eye more than the others – the Liber Pater Society.\n"
"From what you can gather, the society is long-established with a reputation for hosting lavish affairs for the elite.  Many a celebrity and millionaire have been denied membership, the papers eagerly tell, and committees for public morals have often denounced their libertine activities, but never to any real effect.  The few pictures available of their weekly galas depict scenes of Roman decadence, connecting the old cult alibi with modern entertainment of Blake's caliber.  You're in luck that the society meets on Sunday nights."
msgstr ""

msgid "If 1 or more [[Socialite]] or [[Silver Twilight]] investigators were chosen for this campaign:"
msgstr ""

msgid "Upper Echelons"
msgstr ""

msgid "It's hardly your kind of crowd, but you're accustomed to social hobnobbing and prying into hidden affairs.  It's almost a relief from the circus and wilderness."
msgstr ""

msgid "You return to the hotel at once and prepare your best available clothes for the society affair.  Though not exactly formal, Thea's fortune teller robes do fit the old Roman theme of their parties.  She looks in the mirror self-consciously as you converse.  \"I've never been to something so... extravagant.  Or maybe corrupt is more like it.  The Four Leaf Circus wasn't exactly high class, but they had standards.  What about you?  Y'all don't have any... vices, do you?\""
msgstr ""

